## WHAT THE DRAFTER FOUND THAT THE TICKET DID NOT SAY (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER; this is why the lane is larger than "words in a table and one list entry")
1. **The table page cannot be edited by hand.** `docs/ROLE-CAPABILITIES.md` says on its third line "This page is GENERATED. Do not edit it by hand", and test C5 of `__tests__/roles-foundation-route-census.test.js` (`:117`) requires the page to equal the page rendered from `docs/role-capabilities.json`. The Note column is written by `scripts/role-capability-inventory.js` (`notes.push(...)` at `:656-660`); a note can exist only if the generator emits it. So the note's source is a new closed map in the generator, and the two docs files are regenerated by `node scripts/role-capability-inventory.js --generate` (the project's own command; the RD-988 landing did the same, commits `29104c4` and `217c1fe`).
2. **Taking the route off the pending list alone turns two tests red.** `__tests__/rd929-capability-design-census.test.js:59` computes the pending set from the committed inventory (a viewer status that is not 401 or 403, and a capability the viewer does not hold) and requires the list to equal it: this route reads viewer 400 and sits in `feedback.manage` (`capabilities.js:174`), so the census says it IS pending. And `__tests__/rd988-feedback-triage-admin-only.test.js:254` pins that the pending list CONTAINS the route. **Measured:** with only the entry removed, both go red (the census predicate and T7). **The design (Q-1 default) therefore adds a named exception list `OWN_CALLER_CHECK` to `capabilities.js`, the census excuses exactly those routes, and T7's assertion is flipped to `not.toContain`.** The ticket's "line 174 does not change" is kept: the route stays in `feedback.manage` in the table (Q-1 names the alternative that moves it).
3. **A finding to REPORT, not to fix:** the inventory row for this route reads anonymous 401 and `authOrder` "after-global-auth", and `backend/server.js:2238-2241` says the route is deliberately not in the coordinator exempt set. So in an enforced deployment the route's own check (loopback or shared header) is reached only AFTER the sign-in check. The row note says exactly that ("reached after the sign-in check"). Whether the internal coordinator can call it at all in such a deployment is not measured here; report it in READY under OUT OF SCOPE, change nothing.

